cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AETHER in academic work, please cite this software using the metadata below."
title: "AETHER: Adaptive AI Optimization Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "RazorResearch"
    website: "https://github.com/RazorResearch"
abstract: >-
  AETHER is an open research workspace for analysing and optimizing local
  language models. It makes the trade-offs between model intelligence, inference
  speed, VRAM and RAM footprint, and energy consumption explicit and inspectable.
  Version 0.1 is an interface foundation: it ships a navigable desktop-style
  workspace with demonstration data only. No optimization engine, quantization
  pipeline, CUDA kernel or inference runtime is included in this release.
version: "0.1.0-alpha"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RazorResearch/AETHER"
url: "https://github.com/RazorResearch/AETHER"
keywords:
  - "local AI"
  - "language models"
  - "model optimization"
  - "quantization"
  - "inference performance"
  - "memory efficiency"
  - "energy efficiency"
  - "open research"
  - "reproducibility"
